{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-10-01T08:44:03.799Z","data":{"text":"I've completed task 5. Here's a summary of what was implemented:\n\n## Summary\n\n**Routing** (`approve.ts`, `approve-steer.ts`)\n- `approveSpec` now resolves ids with `findSteeringChange`, falling back to `findChange`'s error message when nothing matches.\n- `approveSteeredChange` keeps the running-task refusal first, then routes any change with a default-branch trigger (`isDefaultBranchTrigger`) to the new `approveDefaultBranchSteering`; all other changes keep the 128 path.\n\n**New modules** (`src/core/spec/approve-default-branch*.ts`)\n- `approve-default-branch.ts` — shared prelude: lint, review digest, commit `osq: <id> replanned`, then restart on `conflict` or merge otherwise.\n- `approve-default-branch-restart.ts` — copies the folder aside, removes/recreates the worktree on a fresh branch at the default tip, renames the old branch to `osq/<folder>-restarted-<n>`, trims `.run/` to `events/`+`plan.jsonl`, seals, writes provenance, commits `osq: <id> approved`.\n- `approve-default-branch-merge.ts` — moves archived folders to changes, rebuilds living specs from the default branch, writes `.run/requirements-base`, seals and commits, runs the sync with `skipVerify`, restarts on a `sync_conflict` stop, refreshes merged-scope done markers, and retires triggers.\n\n**CLI** (`cli/approve.ts`) — prints the restart/merge line between `Branch:` and `Continues from task <n>`; extracted `printApprovalResult` to stay within the function budget.\n\n**Tests** (`tests/steering-approve-default-branch.test.ts`) — 6 scenarios in temporary git repos, including the two watcher-driven flows and the `landChange` run.\n\nBoth the task verify (`node --import tsx --test tests/steering-approve-default-branch.test.ts`) and the proposal verify (`pnpm verify`) pass (2911 tests, exit 0). The result is written to `openspec/changes/129-default-branch-steering/.run/results/5.md`."}}
